{"source_record":86,"t":"2026-10-26T16:16:52.171Z","elapsed_s":685.62,"kind":"stop","op":"log","reaction":"I am stopping on the evening of 2 September, after the riders scouts left. This visit I finally found the rule I missed last time, nine passage steps, and planned a passage the game agreed would give six safe places. That felt wonderful. Then for most of two weeks nobody dug the last squares, even with lamps, and every reading just said people may choose another task. I accidentally told Meryem to stop work on the refuge, though she did want a break. Yusuf telling me about the crossed-out passage, and Kian saying I am asleep to the bell, were the best moments. I would not leave it running unattended. I would come back another evening if I could understand why people are not digging my marks, because the plan itself is now a puzzle I care about. I am stopping is selected locally; I typed nothing and pressed no Submit.","game_clock":"Evening · 2 Sep · year 1","engagement":null,"reason":"FRUSTRATED","t_source_lexeme":"\"2026-10-26T16:16:52.171Z\"","elapsed_s_source_lexeme":"685.62","raw_line_sha256":"d5f114b4ed921fd9cc431480ddc1afa5668ae902f39946dbdbcbf1e1f3298e8c"}
